    <h2>10. Expert Tips for Transition Weeks</h2>
    <p>
      Managing clock transitions smoothly requires preparation. Follow these expert recommendations during transition weeks:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Gradual Sleep Adjustments</strong>: Go to bed 15 minutes earlier each night for four days leading up to the spring transition. This minimizes circadian rhythm shock on Monday morning.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Manual Device Audits</strong>: While modern smartphones and computers update their internal clocks automatically, oven timers, wall clocks, and older car dashboards require manual updates. Make a checklist to prevent morning confusion.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Calendar Buffers</strong>: Avoid scheduling critical international business meetings during the two-week gap in March when the US has transitioned to DST but the UK and Europe have not.
      </li>
    </ul>

